WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:04.940
<i>There are three dorms
in Easton Magic Academy.</i>

00:05.350 --> 00:09.780
<i>Students with corresponding characteristics
are assigned to each dorm.</i>

00:12.240 --> 00:14.910
<i>Adler. Courage and conviction.</i>

00:16.320 --> 00:19.080
<i>Orca. Wisdom and willingness.</i>

00:21.250 --> 00:24.000
<i>Lang. Ability and ambition.</i>

00:25.580 --> 00:28.460
<i>The dorms are rivals with one another.</i>

00:28.460 --> 00:31.460
<i>To visualize their principles and positions,</i>

00:31.460 --> 00:34.260
<i>their friendly rivalry
carries across the entire academy.</i>

02:06.430 --> 02:10.020
<i>This is the Adler dorm,
where Mash and Finn reside.</i>

02:10.940 --> 02:13.360
<i>In their room, Room 302...</i>

02:15.480 --> 02:18.780
So, five silver coins make one gold coin?

02:19.410 --> 02:23.660
That's five minus two. Let's see...

02:24.290 --> 02:26.000
Just 28 left.

02:26.330 --> 02:28.460
Five minus two is three.

02:28.460 --> 02:29.750
It's a trick question?

02:29.750 --> 02:32.250
No, there's no tricks about this!

02:32.880 --> 02:34.340
So I'm a meathead?

02:34.340 --> 02:36.880
You got that right, but...

02:39.590 --> 02:43.510
In any case, it's so peaceful today
with nothing going on.

02:44.010 --> 02:45.560
It sure is...

02:47.470 --> 02:49.140
No, there is something!
Our assignment!

02:49.940 --> 02:51.520
Oh. Really?

02:51.520 --> 02:53.900
Crap, crap, I forgot about it!

02:53.900 --> 02:56.190
If we don't submit our Potions assignment,

02:56.190 --> 02:58.780
we'll be severely marked down
and we'll be in the drop-out range!

03:00.950 --> 03:01.950
Want one?

03:02.280 --> 03:04.070
This isn't the time for snacks!

03:04.070 --> 03:05.030
Sorry.

03:05.990 --> 03:10.040
I have to do it! I have to do it!
I have to do my Potions assignment!

03:10.040 --> 03:12.540
You still haven't done it yet?

03:13.330 --> 03:14.590
Lance.

03:15.170 --> 03:16.710
Oh, it's the lolicon.

03:16.710 --> 03:18.050
That's siscon to you.

03:18.510 --> 03:20.760
Loitering around doing nothing...

03:20.760 --> 03:23.590
You two are the dictionary definition
of slackers.

03:23.590 --> 03:26.560
Wait, Lance. Did you finish already?

03:26.680 --> 03:30.060
Of course.
I'm a lot more conscious than you are.

03:30.270 --> 03:34.190
<i>I should've expected that
from the top student in our class.</i>

03:34.190 --> 03:36.070
<i>Lance is simply flawless.</i>

03:36.190 --> 03:40.030
Guys like you
might ruin the dorm's reputation.

03:40.030 --> 03:40.820
Have some shame.

03:48.540 --> 03:50.960
He flew backwards by himself?

03:51.910 --> 03:54.420
<i>O, my precious!</i>

03:54.880 --> 03:57.340
<i>Foisting thy fair light
upon my feeble eyes unwarn’d!</i>

04:00.300 --> 04:02.090
<i>‘Tis my fate to succumb
to thy infinite warmth.</i>

04:02.090 --> 04:03.470
<i>I love you!</i>

04:03.880 --> 04:07.600
You use these for the Potions assignment.

04:07.600 --> 04:10.270
<i>What was with that
dramatic display just now?</i>

04:12.020 --> 04:13.640
A mandragora.

04:14.400 --> 04:19.020
Silence their screams and they become
a universal ingredient in potions.

04:19.440 --> 04:22.190
Oh, another thing that uses magic.

04:22.190 --> 04:25.110
"Another"? You know
this is magic school, right?

04:25.240 --> 04:27.830
I'll show you how it's done.

04:28.490 --> 04:30.040
Quientus.

04:38.840 --> 04:40.000
You try.

04:42.090 --> 04:43.420
Quientus.

04:44.590 --> 04:46.010
Quientus!

04:47.090 --> 04:49.890
I can't do it. It won't stop screaming.

04:49.890 --> 04:51.020
Finn.

04:51.560 --> 04:55.350
Your center of gravity is unstable.
Your core muscles are quite weak.

04:55.350 --> 04:57.150
Huh? Core muscles?

05:01.230 --> 05:02.780
Quientus.

05:07.200 --> 05:11.410
<i>I think it's gotten worse?
Its pupils are dilated, too.</i>

05:11.410 --> 05:14.660
Finn, focus your magic
on a single point.

05:14.910 --> 05:16.290
Oh, okay.

05:16.420 --> 05:17.790
Listen up, Finn.

05:17.790 --> 05:20.960
Visualize gently caressing it
as you release the magic.

05:21.500 --> 05:23.050
O-Okay.

05:23.510 --> 05:25.090
Quientus.

05:26.090 --> 05:29.050
Slowly. That's it.

05:34.520 --> 05:37.480
I did it! I did it, Lance!

05:37.480 --> 05:41.570
Even slackers like you
should be able to do this much.

05:42.480 --> 05:43.940
Thanks!

05:43.940 --> 05:47.070
<i>Maybe Lance is really good
at taking care of others.</i>

05:47.530 --> 05:50.070
Oh, yeah. How is Mash doing?

05:54.870 --> 05:57.710
<i>That plant's flipped out! It's so huge!</i>

06:12.890 --> 06:13.890
I did it.

06:14.220 --> 06:16.390
Did you really, though?

06:20.520 --> 06:23.900
Once they're asleep,
they turn into a regular herb.

06:23.900 --> 06:25.610
Now we create a compound.

06:25.990 --> 06:29.360
Compounding is comparatively simple.
Watch closely.

06:29.950 --> 06:32.620
Take this, and first do this.

06:32.620 --> 06:33.620
Then do this.

06:33.660 --> 06:34.870
And do this.

06:36.160 --> 06:37.370
And with this...

06:38.660 --> 06:39.870
It's done.

06:39.960 --> 06:42.590
<i>That's not easy at all!</i>

06:42.590 --> 06:43.590
Got it.

06:43.590 --> 06:44.880
You've got to be lying!

06:45.210 --> 06:46.380
No, really.

06:47.920 --> 06:49.880
Trust me, as long as it's not magic.

06:50.260 --> 06:51.890
First, take this, and then...

06:52.050 --> 06:53.140
Do this...

06:53.350 --> 06:55.640
Then this... And it's done.

06:57.640 --> 06:59.640
<i>That's totally not it!</i>

06:59.640 --> 07:01.810
<i>How did that end up as a cream puff?</i>

07:01.810 --> 07:03.650
You're screwing around, aren't you?

07:04.190 --> 07:05.650
I'm not screwing around.

07:10.570 --> 07:12.240
You start like this.

07:12.240 --> 07:13.410
'Kay.

07:13.530 --> 07:15.700
Then you add this.

07:15.870 --> 07:16.950
'Kay.

07:16.950 --> 07:18.450
Stir well.

07:18.450 --> 07:19.410
'Kay.

07:19.580 --> 07:21.540
Add this last.

07:21.830 --> 07:22.750
'Kay.

07:23.170 --> 07:23.920
Okay.

07:23.920 --> 07:25.920
BA-YUMMY

07:26.170 --> 07:27.670
<i>Why is this!?</i>

07:28.050 --> 07:30.090
<i>I watched him from start to finish.</i>

07:30.090 --> 07:32.800
<i>When did it become a cream puff!?</i>

07:33.590 --> 07:36.760
You’re completely useless
when not fighting, huh?

07:36.760 --> 07:38.060
Well, yeah.

07:38.270 --> 07:40.680
<i>Why is he so confident?</i>

07:43.310 --> 07:46.190
Oh well. Let me warn you.

07:48.320 --> 07:50.820
I won't lose to you ever again.

07:51.200 --> 07:54.780
There's a reason
I need to join the Bureau of Magic.

07:55.370 --> 07:56.830
And that is?

07:56.830 --> 07:59.330
It's none of your business.

08:01.160 --> 08:05.960
But you equaled me,
if not more, in combat.

08:07.340 --> 08:12.220
I will not allow some nobody
to take your coins away from you.

08:13.050 --> 08:15.430
You don't have to warn me,
because it won't happen.

08:16.640 --> 08:18.560
Quick with the comebacks.

08:18.850 --> 08:20.310
Let's try this again.

08:20.310 --> 08:21.350
'Kay.

08:22.270 --> 08:26.730
The all-dorm off-campus class
is coming up soon.

08:27.060 --> 08:29.730
I wonder if he'll be all right.

08:29.820 --> 08:31.820
And then, that was when...

08:31.820 --> 08:33.650
No way. Are you serious?

08:34.030 --> 08:36.910
And what happened after that?

08:36.910 --> 08:38.280
That's when...

08:39.950 --> 08:42.120
Hey, you bumped into me
just now, didn't you?

08:42.410 --> 08:44.750
Don't be walkin' into people's faces!

08:54.630 --> 08:56.890
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

08:56.890 --> 08:59.760
What am I supposed to do
if I'm not walkin' into people's faces?

09:02.600 --> 09:07.810
Side characters have no right
to give me orders, you moron!

09:11.230 --> 09:14.530
The Divine Visionaries are the ones
who mold this world.

09:15.150 --> 09:17.530
They rule it.

09:18.660 --> 09:21.660
Tell me, what traits
should a ruler possess?

09:21.910 --> 09:26.170
A noble bloodline and overwhelming power
that brooks no argument.

09:27.000 --> 09:30.420
Correct.
Which means it is not those in Adler.

09:34.170 --> 09:36.260
It is us... Lang.

09:38.680 --> 09:41.310
Seize all of their coins.

09:41.430 --> 09:42.680
Yessir.

09:44.020 --> 09:44.930
Nummy.

09:45.100 --> 09:48.520
Ugh, it's tasty? That's a mandragora!

09:48.520 --> 09:49.560
Yum, yum.

09:49.560 --> 09:50.560
Seriously!?

09:51.650 --> 09:55.030
<i>Apparently, mandragora cream puffs are tasty.</i>

09:57.570 --> 09:59.870
<i>And now, the next day...</i>

10:00.490 --> 10:03.790
We're supposed to be
having class here today.

10:03.790 --> 10:05.910
What are we going to do here?

10:06.000 --> 10:08.960
What do you do in a forest...
Camping?

10:08.960 --> 10:12.590
That's for leisure. This is a magic school.

10:12.590 --> 10:14.710
I'm number one!

10:14.800 --> 10:16.670
I'm number one!

10:16.970 --> 10:20.260
I, Dot Barrett,
is the main character of this world!

10:20.260 --> 10:23.060
The world revolves around me!

10:25.390 --> 10:27.480
Whew! It's revolving a bit more than—

10:27.480 --> 10:29.270
Whaddaya think you're looking at!?

10:29.270 --> 10:30.350
Wierdo.

10:30.350 --> 10:32.230
A first-year from our dorm.

10:32.230 --> 10:36.570
Wait, it’s you! The Mushroom Head
people keep talking about!

10:36.990 --> 10:39.410
You look like a side character to me.

10:39.610 --> 10:40.950
Who is this guy?

10:41.160 --> 10:44.740
As of today, you’re a side character
in both name and reality!

10:44.740 --> 10:46.330
Because yours truly is—

10:46.330 --> 10:48.080
Mash!

10:51.750 --> 10:54.590
Outdoor class is a bit scary.

10:54.590 --> 10:59.630
I'm not going to push myself too hard.
So Mash, please take care out there, okay?

10:59.760 --> 11:00.760
Thanks.

11:01.390 --> 11:03.510
Mash, could I possibly tag along—

11:03.510 --> 11:04.720
Hey.

11:10.810 --> 11:11.980
I'll kill 'im!

11:13.150 --> 11:17.820
I friggin' hate guys
who get attention from women!

11:17.820 --> 11:19.990
I'll kill you! I'll triple kill ya!

11:20.150 --> 11:22.490
It's ridiculous to begin with!

11:22.740 --> 11:25.330
The global ratio of men to women
is supposed to be equal!

11:25.330 --> 11:28.500
So why isn't there a single girl
falling in love with me!?

11:28.660 --> 11:30.500
That's right, the answer is simple.

11:30.750 --> 11:34.000
It's because chumps like you
ruin the system!

11:34.290 --> 11:38.210
Guys like you are why we have
an aging population and a lower birthrate!

11:38.210 --> 11:40.010
Won't someone just settle for me!?

11:40.010 --> 11:42.010
That's why I made up my mind!

11:42.300 --> 11:46.760
I'm gonna join the Bureau of Magic
and rid this world of hot guys!

11:47.100 --> 11:47.810
- Oh Mash, I'll totally marry you.
- Do cream puffs count as snacks?

11:47.810 --> 11:49.930
That mandragora cream puff
was tasty, huh?
- Oh Mash, I'll totally marry you.
- Do cream puffs count as snacks?

11:49.930 --> 11:51.060
- Oh Mash, I'll totally marry you.
- Do cream puffs count as snacks?

11:52.190 --> 11:53.350
Listen to me!

11:53.350 --> 11:56.360
My ego gets bruised the most
when I'm ignored!

11:56.360 --> 11:58.280
Quiet, all of you.

12:00.900 --> 12:05.120
Both Adler and Lang will participate
in this outdoor exercise.

12:05.120 --> 12:08.950
Your reward will be either a bronze or silver coin.
Brace yourselves.

12:11.870 --> 12:14.670
Your task is the extermination
of forest scorpions.

12:15.330 --> 12:18.420
Bring me the stones
embedded in their foreheads.

12:18.840 --> 12:22.340
Most forest scorpions
will only earn you bronze coins,

12:22.550 --> 12:26.930
but a few are strong enough
to be worth silver coins.

12:27.140 --> 12:29.140
You can identify them easily.

12:29.850 --> 12:33.230
If the stone in their foreheads
are square, they're worth silvers.

12:33.350 --> 12:36.860
Ordinary magic users
almost certainly don't stand a chance.

12:38.110 --> 12:42.110
But such accomplishments
make you Easton students.

12:42.530 --> 12:44.570
Do what you must to survive.

12:45.030 --> 12:47.780
In you go, in order now.

12:50.240 --> 12:53.870
Yeah, it's on!
No way I'm losing to you!

12:56.130 --> 12:59.380
I'd like to make sure to get silver coins here.

12:59.840 --> 13:01.380
I should do my best, too.

13:05.430 --> 13:08.720
You think you're hot stuff, right?

13:08.850 --> 13:11.470
I can tell.

13:11.560 --> 13:14.560
You think you're so special.

13:14.560 --> 13:18.860
You mistakenly think
you're not like the others.

13:19.270 --> 13:22.440
You subconsciously
look down on others, don't you?

13:26.700 --> 13:28.490
Hey, what are you doing over there?

13:28.740 --> 13:29.870
I'll mark you down for that.

13:29.870 --> 13:34.370
Sorry, Professor.
We were just horsing around.

13:34.500 --> 13:36.370
Right, first-year?

13:38.420 --> 13:40.790
Yes, yes. That's the look.

13:40.790 --> 13:44.220
I want to make
a pathetically messed up face outta you.

13:44.720 --> 13:47.590
Looking forward to it, first-year!

13:48.550 --> 13:49.720
Hey, Mash.

13:50.720 --> 13:52.350
Ignore him.

13:52.680 --> 13:54.980
He's one year older than us.

13:54.980 --> 13:57.980
And he's infamous for misconduct.

13:58.480 --> 14:02.650
He's injured multiple teachers
and students he doesn't like,

14:02.650 --> 14:04.740
to the point of being held back a grade.

14:05.530 --> 14:11.080
But they consider his talent as a magic user,
so they haven't expelled him yet.

14:11.830 --> 14:14.370
You hear stuff like that often
from Lang dorm.

14:14.750 --> 14:16.710
So, don't bother with them.

14:16.710 --> 14:17.870
I'm glad.

14:18.120 --> 14:20.500
I thought he crushed my cream puff.

14:21.210 --> 14:25.010
<i>That's why he made that face?</i>

14:26.010 --> 14:30.090
And don't tuck food in there directly.
It's unhygienic.

14:30.090 --> 14:31.140
'Kay.

14:33.930 --> 14:36.390
I smell tremendous danger.

14:36.890 --> 14:40.100
I think it's wiser for us to work as a pair.

14:40.230 --> 14:42.110
Leave it to me, the oldest son...

14:46.570 --> 14:49.320
I zoned out, and now I'm all alone.

14:50.530 --> 14:51.490
Oh well.

14:51.490 --> 14:54.870
Yo yo yo, get those tails on out,
damned scorpions!

14:55.290 --> 14:57.870
I'm gonna show up that mushroom head—

15:03.040 --> 15:04.630
Shut up.

15:07.170 --> 15:11.300
Just now, I wasted calories because of you.

15:11.300 --> 15:13.100
This is just terrible.

15:13.100 --> 15:14.350
I'll kill 'im.

15:14.600 --> 15:17.770
Fine. Forget about our class.

15:17.770 --> 15:19.270
Right here right now, you're...

15:21.230 --> 15:22.310
Stop it!

15:22.310 --> 15:23.400
Shut up!

15:23.400 --> 15:25.400
Because of you, I...

15:26.110 --> 15:27.900
I'll make you regret it!

15:28.490 --> 15:32.030
S-Someone... Someone help me!

15:32.490 --> 15:33.530
Explomb.

15:45.920 --> 15:50.010
Raising your hand against a girl...
You're so done as a guy.

15:50.930 --> 15:52.380
U-Um...

15:52.380 --> 15:53.180
Huh?

15:54.760 --> 15:56.560
Thank you so much.

15:58.520 --> 16:01.690
<i>S-S-S-So beautiful!</i>

16:02.440 --> 16:06.570
<i>Nope. Play it cool!
I have to stay calm and act natural!</i>

16:10.820 --> 16:13.490
That was nothing at...

16:14.070 --> 16:17.240
<i>H-H-Her hands... So soft...</i>

16:18.790 --> 16:21.960
You're... so strong.

16:23.790 --> 16:26.040
Argh! I can't do it!

16:37.140 --> 16:40.930
Now, is it almost time?

16:44.980 --> 16:48.020
Thank you so much for what you did earlier.

16:48.440 --> 16:50.860
I-It was nothing.

16:51.940 --> 16:54.450
<i>O-O-Our knees are touching!</i>

16:54.950 --> 16:58.160
<i>So, this is the natural distance
of a modern couple?</i>

16:58.160 --> 17:01.450
<i>Stay calm. Be still, my heart.</i>

17:01.450 --> 17:03.960
<i>If I act weird, she'll catch on
that I'm unpopular with girls.</i>

17:03.960 --> 17:06.670
<i>Keep cool. Come on, me. Keep cool.</i>

17:07.210 --> 17:08.710
Cool! Cool! Cool!

17:10.550 --> 17:12.460
What's with him? Freaky.

17:12.840 --> 17:14.680
Huh? What'd you just say?

17:14.680 --> 17:17.760
I was marveling at how
manly and wonderful you are.

17:18.050 --> 17:19.640
Oh no, I actually said wonderful.

17:19.640 --> 17:22.060
Huh? I thought I heard two syllables.

17:22.060 --> 17:23.230
It's the truth.

17:25.060 --> 17:27.730
You really are wonderful.

17:35.860 --> 17:40.700
<i>With my magic, I can make anyone
even slightly attracted to me fall in love.</i>

17:41.160 --> 17:43.870
<i>He's completely fallen for me now.</i>

17:44.120 --> 17:47.290
<i>Though, maybe he might
have fallen even without magic.</i>

17:48.000 --> 17:50.630
<i>Next up, that mushroom head...</i>

17:51.130 --> 17:55.510
Thank you too, kind sir.
You were a great help.

17:55.510 --> 17:58.260
Oh, I didn't do anything.

17:59.180 --> 18:00.760
<i>What? That's impossible.</i>

18:01.260 --> 18:04.770
<i>There's never been a man
who hasn't fallen under my spell.</i>

18:05.020 --> 18:09.770
<i>More like, any guy should be like “hurray!”
if a cute girl like me was flirting with him.</i>

18:10.900 --> 18:13.280
<i>I'll have to put more magic energy into it.</i>

18:14.490 --> 18:16.280
That's not true.

18:16.280 --> 18:18.240
You really helped me out.

18:18.740 --> 18:20.740
You're very wonderful.

18:21.120 --> 18:26.080
<i>Sound, sight, touch.
My charm reaches all the senses!</i>

18:26.500 --> 18:29.290
<i>There is no man who can resist this!</i>

18:31.710 --> 18:34.670
I said, I didn't do anything.

18:35.460 --> 18:38.430
<i>It's not working at all!?
What is wrong with this guy?</i>

18:38.430 --> 18:41.550
<i>Does he seriously
not find me attractive!? Die!</i>

18:42.010 --> 18:45.930
<i>Fine. It's ours for the taking
now that I have one of theirs.</i>

18:46.730 --> 18:49.350
But you really did save me.

18:50.810 --> 18:53.230
<i>Such a delicate facial expression.</i>

18:54.860 --> 18:58.450
Do you have some kind of circumstance?
I'll lend an ear.

18:58.650 --> 19:02.450
Actually, there’s a certain boy
threatening me.

19:02.450 --> 19:03.780
A certain boy?

19:04.200 --> 19:06.910
A second-year by the name of Silva.

19:06.910 --> 19:10.330
He's someone I don't hear
many good things about.

19:10.330 --> 19:13.590
He's trying to take advantage
of magic only I can use.

19:13.590 --> 19:16.090
He's been stalking me for all this time.

19:16.710 --> 19:20.590
I don't want to be involved
in anything that’s bad.

19:20.760 --> 19:23.550
But he's forcing me to, like he did earlier.

19:24.810 --> 19:28.730
I don't know what I should do.

19:32.350 --> 19:34.980
I'm sorry to bring this up so suddenly.

19:35.400 --> 19:39.280
It's all right.
I'm totally gonna beat that guy up.

19:39.400 --> 19:42.320
Oh no.
Please don't go out of your way.

19:42.660 --> 19:46.540
No. He's definitely
getting beaten to a pulp.

19:47.580 --> 19:49.000
Kind sir...

19:49.460 --> 19:50.870
Hey!

19:56.500 --> 19:59.760
Who's gonna beat who to a pulp?

19:59.760 --> 20:00.630
Huh?

20:00.760 --> 20:02.090
So you're the guy...

20:02.090 --> 20:04.640
I'll be the one to kill you.

20:06.180 --> 20:09.640
You look like the cringiest punk out there.

20:09.890 --> 20:16.520
Whenever I come across a deluded loser
like you, I can't help but give them a dose of reality.

20:17.110 --> 20:21.360
And when I do, what kind of look
will you have on your face?

20:21.360 --> 20:22.400
Explomb!

20:33.000 --> 20:35.500
Machine Gun Explomb!

20:37.630 --> 20:39.260
I'm not done yet!

20:39.260 --> 20:41.170
Oi oi oi oi!

20:41.170 --> 20:42.720
Explomb!

20:52.730 --> 20:54.440
Die twice!

20:56.770 --> 20:58.440
<i>Meanwhile...</i>

21:00.900 --> 21:03.650
- I'm so glad you’re with us.
- I’m so scared!

21:03.650 --> 21:04.450
Let go.

21:04.700 --> 21:07.120
Don't leave us!

21:08.120 --> 21:11.500
- Please don't! No! Don't leave us!
- You’re the only one we can rely on!
<i>Anyway, is he doing all right?</i>

21:11.500 --> 21:11.790
- Please don't! No! Don't leave us!
- You’re the only one we can rely on!

21:11.790 --> 21:14.330
<i>It seems that second-year
was targeting him.</i>
- Please don't! No! Don't leave us!
- You’re the only one we can rely on!

21:14.830 --> 21:17.290
<i>They haven’t run into each other, have they?</i>

21:17.880 --> 21:20.590
Heh! You weren't much of anything!

21:27.260 --> 21:32.100
Your puny magic
can't break through mine.

21:32.310 --> 21:33.430
Got it!?

21:38.810 --> 21:44.110
Hey hey, what's wrong now?
Where'd all that energy go?

21:44.450 --> 21:46.360
You're gonna kill me, right?

21:46.360 --> 21:49.410
Why don't you try a bit harder?

21:49.780 --> 21:51.790
But it's no wonder!

21:51.790 --> 21:54.120
Because even a moron can tell
the difference...

21:54.120 --> 21:57.670
once they've seen the difference
in our skills!
